Feats are a good idea, but of course the preliminary list 
contains some imperfections which others have pointed out.

It seems to me that some feats could have negative "rewards".
The point would be that achieving the goal of "Featful conduct"
should not be merely a process of gathering small rewards.

Null rewards are also a possibility, though in some cases your
reward is already "a chance of getting foo".

In any case, when people point out that one of the proposed 
rewards is fairly useless, the above reasoning allows you to
reply by saying "So what?"

Eating a footrice corpse and surviving -- what an excellent 
use for those excess amulets of life saving, or an excellent
reason to polyself into a stoning-resistant monster!

